BND-17: keep the time of the daily maximum temperature after sunrise

updateTempTimes() puts the daily minimum temperature at sunrise and the
maximum 3 h before sunset. When the day is shorter than 3 h (polar winter,
where the sunrise hour angle is clamped to 0) the maximum comes before
sunrise, the rising branch of the interpolation is never used, the
temperature jumps at sunrise and never reaches Tmax. For days shorter than
4 h the rise is also squeezed into less than an hour. Keep the hour of the
maximum at least 1 h after sunrise. Days of 4 h or longer are unchanged.

Apply from the root of a Stormwater-Management-Model checkout at cb3e192b:
    git apply BND-17_swmm530.patch

diff --git a/src/legacy/engine/climate.c b/src/legacy/engine/climate.c
index c343b93..3213c07 100644
--- a/src/legacy/engine/climate.c
+++ b/src/legacy/engine/climate.c
@@ -1327,6 +1327,12 @@ void updateTempTimes(int day)
     hrang = 3.8197 * arg;
     Hrsr = 12.0 - hrang + Temp.dtlong;
     Hrss = 12.0 + hrang + Temp.dtlong - 3.0;
+
+    // --- for days shorter than 4 h (polar winter) the max. temp. hour
+    //     would come less than 1 h after, or even before, the min. temp.
+    //     hour at sunrise; keep it 1 h after sunrise
+    if (Hrss < Hrsr + 1.0)
+        Hrss = Hrsr + 1.0;
     Dhrdy = Hrsr - Hrss;
     Dydif = 24.0 + Hrsr - Hrss;
     Hrday = (Hrsr + Hrss) / 2.0;
